contentText:
SB19 talks about performing &#8220;Lawless&#8221; at Lollapalooza, being the first Filipino group to perform at the Chicago festival, giving the fans a little taste of their song for the upcoming Dreamworks animated movie Forgotten Island , performing at the Grammy Museum and who they&#8217;re excited to watch at Lollapalooza while they&#8217;re at the festival.

Tetris Kelly&nbsp;&nbsp;

All right, hanging out. I should probably call the police because I&#8217;m with some &#8220;Lawless&#8221; guys. What&#8217;s up, SB19? Yo,

SB19&nbsp;

What&#8217;s up? We are SB19 from the Philippines. Let&#8217;s go!

Alright, so you guys got to perform &#8220;Lawless&#8221; for Lollapalooza tonight, the brand new single. How was that?

Pablo&nbsp;

It was great.&nbsp;

Stell&nbsp;

Yeah, it was great.

It&#8217;s the first time that we ever performed that song, and then we just released that like a few hours ago. So, like when we when we when I was performing earlier, like my mind went blank. Like, just had to move. You know, it&#8217;s Lollapalooza, and there are lots of people watching, so had to move.

Man, you guys are dropping the music video as well. So how was it to do the creative behind this song? Because it&#8217;s like so raw. It&#8217;s a really fun song.

Justin&nbsp;

Yeah, basically we just need to be &#8220;Lawless&#8221; and you know show the world how chaotic we are because that&#8217;s that&#8217;s being authentic and we want it to be authentic, so that&#8217;s it. Let&#8217;s go, Lawlesspalooza.

Josh&nbsp;

If you&#8217;ve noticed that there&#8217;s a symbolism, it&#8217;s a goat, because it means goated.

Tetris Kelly&nbsp;

I mean, you guys are goated, especially the vocals. You know, I was giving you a hard time about time, but time, the vocals, 10 out of 10. And then you guys also previewed a little special moment for your song from the DreamWorks movie. So how was that to debut the?

Stell&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;

Well, of course, we would like to thank DreamWorks for giving us opportunity to sing one of the legendary song from the rapper in the Philippines, Sir Francis Magalona. We&#8217;re very honored to do that. But of course, yes, doing an official soundtrack for Forgotten Island is something that we&#8217;re very proud of, and we think that we hope we give justice to the song, and we&#8217;re very excited for the fans to hear it, and of course, we&#8217;re very excited to to see the film, and we hope to see it together while we were here in the U.S. maybe.

